All trades are going to essentially become highly trained and specialized QA/Architect types. This is already starting to happen in software, and it is going to spread everywhere over the next few years. SWEs are spending most of their time driving architectural tweaks in AI code, then manually testing those changes to cover edge cases. Some fields will take longer than others.

Engineers, Lawyers, Doctors, Finance/Accounting, Sales/Marketing, Plumbers/Electricians. Machine Drivers.

The people who survive will be trained and specialized and experienced enough to be architects, directing AI work, and QAs, checking AI work before it "goes live." People will gain experience by being given "architecture/QA" positions over elements that are small and insignificant. 

Eg: "This job will focus on the quality and design of tasks that AI agents use to execute lawn mowing functions."

